{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"datum as representation datum as representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md","fileName":"Datum as Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Datum as Representation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 09:02\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Science Framing and Representation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Framing and Representation","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"datum as representation datum as representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Datum as Representation.md","fileName":"Datum as Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Datum as Representation","heading":"Datum as Representation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A datum is a recorded representation of some aspect of the world, not the aspect itself. A row may stand for a customer, transaction, or event, but the selected fields capture only the properties that collection systems could observe and that analysts chose to retain.\n\nThis distinction matters when interpreting results. A model learns relationships among recorded attributes; omitted circumstances and measurement choices remain outside its view. Treating the dataset as a partial abstraction encourages domain checks before a statistical pattern is converted into a claim about people or causes.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Framing and Representation","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/D